# Quick Reference

## Commands

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build
dotnet run
dotnet test
dotnet run -c Release

dotnet run -- path\to\file.txt
dotnet run -- missing-new.txt      # empty buffer; Save creates file
dotnet run -- path\to\folder       # open workspace

dotnet build -c Release && bun link   # global xpad → Release xpad.exe
xpad --help
```

```powershell
pwsh scripts/publish-win-x64.ps1
pwsh scripts/publish-win-x64.ps1 -Mode selfcontained
pwsh scripts/publish-msix.ps1 -Install
pwsh scripts/release.ps1
pwsh scripts/smoke-cli.ps1
pwsh scripts/smoke-single-instance.ps1
pwsh scripts/smoke-workspace.ps1
```

## Important paths

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `Views/`, `ViewModels/`, `Services/`, `Editor/`, `Models/` | App layers |
| `x-pad.Tests/` | xUnit |
| `scripts/` | Publish, MSIX, smoke, release |
| `packaging/windows/AppxManifest.xml` | MSIX template |
| `%APPDATA%/XPad/` | settings, session, layout, recovery, crash.log |

## Stack

- .NET 10 / C# nullable
- Avalonia 12 + AvaloniaEdit + TextMateSharp
- CommunityToolkit.Mvvm
- Iciclecreek.Avalonia.Terminal (ConPTY)
- QuestPDF (export), System.Drawing.Common (print on Windows)

## Patterns to remember

1. `TextDocument` per tab; dirty via UndoStack
2. I/O only through `FileService`
3. Keybindings via catalog/applier
4. Optional LSP/AI — fail soft

